+
+Evidence: obligation report `runs/checks/1793500312489856031/results.json`; final report `runs/checks/1793500403902337952/results.json`. Every formal configuration uses the fixed caller, actual Cargo source and all imported bodies under --no-cheating. These passes establish the bounded local contracts; they do not establish global implementation acceptance or replace semantic review.
+
+The invariant requires valid persistent state, pending actions consistent with that state, uniqueness of the recorded choices, and bounds relating every choice to the current term/vote. Recovery also establishes a lower bound at the retained term and preserves its chosen candidate at that term. Real operations preserve these facts. The fixed observer records accepted campaign self-choices before completion and affirmative replies from actual completion results. The composition proof combines arbitrary actual prefixes and suffixes across both specified successful-write windows without inventing an old completion. A self-choice is neither durable I/O evidence nor a counted vote.
+
+Passing tests cover receiver rejection priority and log freshness, repeated same-candidate votes, higher-term denials, shared campaign/receiver state, exhaustion, wrong/duplicate completion, halting on failed save, real candidate-to-two-receiver RPCs, delayed save, file byte contents, malformed storage, confirmed receiver recovery, both self-vote recovery windows and no single-member promotion. The written-pending receiver test reaches and passes retained-file/recovered-state assertions before failing on its observer check; its later post-recovery RPC assertions are not reached. Formal receiver pending recovery nevertheless passes.
+
+Protected-test contradiction: `tasks/election_start/rpc_tests.rs:188` creates the observation channel; the task receives its sole sender. At line 203 the test aborts and awaits that task, dropping the sender without sending a reply. At line 213 it asserts that `timeout(..., observed.recv()).await.is_err()`. Empty closed-channel receive returns Err immediately, so timeout returns Ok(Err), making this assertion false even with no old reply. The same failure occurs on all five seeds. The independent diagnostic `madraft/repro/closed_observer.rs` polls the actual pinned channel after dropping a future owning its only sender and observes Ready(Err). Its output is retained in `madraft/repro/closed_observer.log`. A correct no-message observer must distinguish channel closure from a delivered value; the protected test has been left intact. The Core neither owns nor receives this channel, so repairing its lifetime would require changing protected test/host behavior or an unrelated workaround.
+
+Unverified host premises: serialized receive/save/complete and campaign/save/complete calls; actual write results reported truthfully; retained bytes read back equal to the emitted Record in the bounded recovery windows; encoding/decoding preserve values; configured membership/address mapping and requester identity are correct; authorized replies and immutable requests are forwarded unchanged; cancellation releases the old Core before recovery. Exact functions are vote_host::{encode,decode,load,checkpoint,save}, RaftHandle::{new_receiver,start_rpc_server,request_vote,start_election,send_vote_request}, and the mutex/task/network/filesystem operations they call. Core validation discharges domain checks without assuming valid external data; protocol decisions and authorization remain in the verified Core. The async host itself is not formally verified. MadSim completed-write retention and sync_all do not prove real-disk power-loss durability. The Rust/Verus/vstd/SMT toolchain and ghost erasure remain trusted.
